# Local device and signing settings. Copy to ios/local.env (ignored by git) and fill in; ~/.config/dm-ios/local.env works too and can be shared
# by several working trees.
# The game to build (games/<id>/game.json)
DM_GAME=manosaba
# devicectl identifier of the device: the Identifier column of `xcrun devicectl list devices` (install / launch / log / push-data)
DM_DEVICE=
# Hardware UDID of the device (Xcode → Devices and Simulators → Identifier). Needed with a free account: the build targets this phone, which must
# be connected, before Apple creates a provisioning profile for a free team
DM_IOS_UDID=
# Signing: the Team ID of your team (Xcode → Settings → Accounts) and your own bundle ID (reverse domain, e.g. org.example.mygame).
# The iCloud container is derived from it (iCloud.<bundle ID>)
DM_TEAM_ID=
DM_BUNDLE_ID=
# 1 for a free developer account (personal team): the build leaves out the entitlements it cannot sign (iCloud save sync, sustained execution,
# increased memory limit, extended virtual addressing). Free accounts: profiles expire after 7 days (rebuild and reinstall), at most 3 devices and
# 3 apps per device; trust the developer in Settings → General → VPN & Device Management before the first launch
DM_FREE_ACCOUNT=
